          <h2>The benefit categories behind WellFinder treatments</h2>
          <p>Manulife group plans handle most wellness care as paramedical claims. The claim pays toward treatment from a recognized practitioner, and the practitioner type on your receipt decides which category the visit draws from. The categories that matter most for WellFinder readers are:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Naturopathy, which covers microneedling, IV and IM vitamin therapy and fertility consultations with a naturopathic doctor</li>
            <li>Physiotherapy, which covers pelvic floor physiotherapy, vestibular rehabilitation, shockwave therapy and running gait analysis</li>
            <li>Chiropractic, which some clinical Pilates and golf assessment clinics bill under</li>
            <li>Massage therapy, which covers TMJ massage, lymphatic drainage and pressotherapy given by a registered massage therapist</li>
            <li>Acupuncture, which covers fertility acupuncture, cosmetic acupuncture and facial gua sha from a registered acupuncturist</li>
            <li>Psychology and psychotherapy, which cover couples therapy, neurofeedback and sleep coaching</li>
            <li>Speech therapy, which covers singing voice therapy, accent modification and stuttering therapy</li>
            <li>Dietitian services, which cover sports nutrition consultations with a registered dietitian</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Plans differ in which categories they include and how much they pay. Annual maximums per category are typical, and many plans limit the amount paid per visit. Practitioners need to be licensed or registered in their province, and that detail needs to appear on your receipt.</p>

          <h2>How claiming works with Manulife</h2>
          <p>Members claim on the Manulife plan member site at manulife.ca/planmember or in the Manulife Mobile app, signing in with a Manulife ID. You choose the claim type, enter the provider and the date of service, and attach a photo or scan of your receipt. The Coverage and balances view in the app and on the site shows what remains under each category, along with your spending account balances, so you can check before you book and again after you claim. To keep claims moving:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Set up direct deposit so payments land in your bank account</li>
            <li>Keep the receipt from every visit, showing the practitioner, their licence or registration, the date and the amount</li>
            <li>Submit soon after the visit, and keep an eye on the claim status in the app</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Direct billing is common with Manulife plans. As Manulife explains in its member questions, if your provider offers direct billing, the provider can submit the claim on your behalf, and you pay only the portion your plan does not cover. Ask the clinic when you book, since the clinic needs to be set up to bill Manulife and your plan needs to allow it.</p>
          <p>If your provider or service does not appear in the online claim tool, you can still choose the options for a service not listed or a provider not listed, or use a paper claim form from the plan member site.</p>

          <h2>Health care and wellness spending accounts</h2>
          <p>Many Manulife plans pair the main coverage with a Health Care Spending Account, often shortened to HCSA. The account holds an amount set by your employer, and you can claim eligible health and dental expenses against it, following the list the Canada Revenue Agency allows. The usual order is to claim under your main plan first, then claim any amount left over against the HCSA.</p>
          <p>Some Manulife plans also include a Wellness Spending Account, sometimes called a WSA or a lifestyle account, for costs such as fitness memberships and sports activities. Money from a wellness account is generally a taxable benefit. Balances for both accounts show in the app and on the plan member site, and spending account claims go through the same online claim flow.</p>

          <h2>WellFinder treatments and how they may bill under a Manulife plan</h2>
          <p>Costs below are typical Canadian prices collected for the WellFinder directory. Your plan pays according to its own maximums, so confirm the amounts for each category in the app.</p>
