          <h2>Questions members ask</h2>
          <h3>Does Manulife cover naturopath visits?</h3>
          <p>Many Manulife group plans include naturopathy as a paramedical category, with an annual maximum. The visit needs to be with a naturopathic doctor who is registered in your province, and the receipt needs to show that registration. Check your own category list in the app, since some leaner plans leave naturopathy out.</p>
          <h3>Can my clinic bill Manulife directly?</h3>
          <p>Often, yes. Providers set up with Manulife can submit the claim while you are at the clinic, and you pay only the part your plan does not cover. Bring your benefit card details or the app so the clinic has your plan contract number and member certificate number.</p>
          <h3>What should I do when my main plan pays only part of a visit?</h3>
          <p>If your plan includes a Health Care Spending Account, claim the remaining amount against the account once the main claim is settled. Keep the claim statement from the first claim, since the spending account claim may ask for it as proof of what was already paid.</p>
          <h3>Do I need a referral for physiotherapy or massage therapy?</h3>
          <p>Most members book these practitioners directly. A minority of plans ask for a physician note before paying certain paramedical claims, and your plan booklet is the place that states it.</p>

          <h2>Find care that fits your Manulife plan</h2>
          <p>Match the treatment to the category, then check your balance. Browse the <a href="/#directory">WellFinder directory</a> to compare clinics across Canada, and open pages such as <a href="/naturopath">naturopath clinics</a> and <a href="/clinics-couples-therapy">couples therapy clinics</a> to see who provides each treatment. Before you book, sign in to the Manulife app to confirm the category is part of your plan and ask the clinic how the visit will be billed.</p>
          <p>WellFinder is an independent directory and is not affiliated with Manulife. This guide explains common features of Manulife group plans in Canada. Your employer plan governs your coverage, and Manulife or your plan administrator can confirm what your plan pays.</p>

